---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';

const path = '/guides';
const title = 'Cart recovery decision guides';
const desc = 'Start with the operating problem, then decide whether software needs to change.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="container py-16 md:py-24">
<a class="link" href="/">Explore related guides</a>
<h1 class="hero-title mt-6">Cart recovery decision guides</h1>
<p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9">Start with the operating problem, then decide whether software needs to change.</p>
<article class="prose-shopify mt-12 max-w-4xl">
<h2>Choose a reading path</h2>
<p>For a first workflow, use the <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">abandoned-cart implementation guide</a>. For a category-specific constraint, open <a class="link" href="/for">store types</a>. For a replacement decision, use <a class="link" href="/compare">comparisons</a>. This hub organizes questions; it does not report merchant tests or certify every linked page.</p>
<h2>Timing and channel mix</h2>
<p>Write down the observed time between departure and return, the question a reminder answers, and which channel can reach the eligible shopper. Compare a useful reminder against the existing path before adding another touch. Choose recipient timing with the responsible regional reviewer; do not treat a generic quiet-hours window as worldwide legal guidance. Record who owns cart, checkout, welcome and subscription messages.</p>
<h2>Incentive governance</h2>
<p>Document which costs change when a recovered order is placed: goods, fulfillment, shipping subsidy, payment and channel fees, discounts and expected returns. Set a contribution floor with finance. Check welcome and loyalty offers for stacking. An assistance-only path is a useful baseline; it is not proof that every discount harms the business.</p>
<h2>Checkout friction and inventory</h2>
<p>Investigate shipping quote, payment failure, account requirements and product uncertainty separately. A message cannot repair a broken payment step. Inspect the actual selected variant and current availability before returning a shopper to checkout. For a partially unavailable basket, explain the missing item and preserve shopper choice rather than silently substituting.</p>
<h2>Attribution and experiments</h2>
<p>Define the eligible population and order window before comparison. A randomized holdout can estimate additional orders, but its size depends on traffic and the effect being measured. Keep offer, timing and channel changes separable. Report contribution, opt-outs and returns alongside orders; attributed revenue alone does not establish causation.</p>
<h2>Consent and message ownership</h2>
<p>Have the responsible reviewer document the permissions and rules for each channel and market. Preserve permission source and withdrawals across migration. Assign one system to each event, document purchase exits and support pauses, and inspect queued messages when a shopper moves from cart to checkout. Platform configuration is not a legal determination.</p>
<h2>Turn the decision into a handoff</h2>
<p>Give the operator an event definition, data fields, exclusion rules, approved content, owner, rollback condition and measurement window. Ask finance to review incentive costs and support to review pause behavior. A proposed rehearsal should include purchase in another session, missing permission and an unavailable line; save the observed evidence before enabling it.</p>
<h2>Review what changed</h2>
<p>Revisit the affected record when a supplier changes an event, the catalog changes fulfillment terms, or a new channel is introduced. Date the decision and keep the previous version so a replacement owner can reconstruct why the rule exists. No fixed annual calendar or arbitrary test duration can substitute for that evidence.</p>
</article>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
